### Compatible update, installation and baseline lock-metadata normalization

The preserved lock comes exclusively from npm 10.9.2's ordinary targeted
`npm update npm google-auth-library gaxios --package-lock-only --ignore-scripts --engine-strict`
(exit 0); there are no hand-edits of the lock. Fresh registry metadata and installed parent
artifacts confirm @google/genai 2.10.0 → google-auth-library `^10.3.0`,
google-auth-library 10.9.1 → gaxios `^7.1.4`, and @semantic-release/npm 13.1.5 → npm
`^11.6.2`; semver checks accept the exact targets below.

| Updated installed path | Before → after | Candidate registry artifact integrity (SHA-512) |
|---|---|---|
| `node_modules/google-auth-library` | 10.6.1 → 10.9.1 | `sha512-i1ydyHrqcIxXkWh/uBmVkzCvIuq5yiK2ATndIe5XxKholrG/MTYP9xGYka4sQhrbIAgGjL2B6NOE7rFaiF3fXw==` |
| `node_modules/gaxios` | 7.1.3 → 7.3.1 | `sha512-kB3rzJV7d9juLZh8/56QTXCwQfxyhdOMdyYk1HdQKFtF8TJTDTZQJtixWIwXdE9Jji91mC41DUNpjleo4L4eAQ==` |
| `node_modules/npm` | 11.21.1 → 11.21.2 | `sha512-7HPApk+AflMUavSseL1Pm6CnYqMIHk53x+KmuhqmTDqPkjPMgxIpTPcTqsE91EKNw4gFBJV9fnXiSdGm1DXq9A==` |

Resolved URLs are the corresponding `https://registry.npmjs.org/<name>/-/<name>-<version>.tgz`
artifacts. The lock integrities agree with freshly fetched registry metadata. npm ci verifies
the parent artifact; nested `inBundle: true` entries are proven by the actual installed npm
bundle, not inferred from unrelated top-level packages.

Required bundle changes beneath `node_modules/npm/node_modules/`: @npmcli/promise-spawn
9.0.1 → 9.0.2, bin-links 6.0.2 → 6.0.3, ip-address 10.7.2 → 10.7.5, libnpmexec
10.3.4 → 10.3.5, pacote 21.5.1 → 21.5.2, semver 7.8.5 → 7.8.6, undici 6.29.0 → 6.29.1.
These are npm 11.21.2's bundled contents. gaxios drops its rimraf edge; the resulting `dev: true`
changes apply only to the former rimraf/glob cleanup subtree (29 entries), with no resolution
changes there. Google SDK, semantic-release, direct minimatch, rimraf and TypeDoc versions
are unchanged. Every third-party change belongs to these targeted parent updates.

**Baseline lock-metadata normalization:** npm's ordinary write synchronizes exactly the
three workspace version fields (`packages/cli`, `packages/llmist`, `packages/testing`)
from `18.4.0` to their unchanged manifests' `18.4.1`, and exactly these four internal ranges
from `^18.4.0` to `^18.4.1`:

- `packages/cli` dependencies `llmist`;
- `packages/cli` devDependencies `@llmist/testing`;
- `packages/testing` devDependencies `llmist`;
- `packages/testing` peerDependencies `llmist`.

The operator explicitly authorizes these seven lock metadata fields as a required graph
change. No other workspace-entry field changes; no manifest changes. This is metadata
normalization, not a version bump or release, and causes no third-party resolution change.
The four `node_modules/{llmist,@llmist/cli,@llmist/testing,@llmist/docs}` entries remain
`link: true` and resolve to their respective `packages/*` directories. A structural comparison
checks these exact allowances and byte-compares every tracked manifest against the base.

`npm ci --engine-strict --ignore-scripts=false` passes on the candidate (exit 0, 10.19 s),
with no lock mutation. Direct `node_modules/.bin/lefthook install` succeeds; executable
pre-commit, commit-msg and pre-push hooks all invoke Lefthook. Root postinstall and prepare
output contains no hidden lifecycle error; `@unblessed/core/dist/data` is a working symlink
to `../data`. Baseline installation also passes (exit 0, 9.65 s).

