### Residual interpretation: AC #3 manual protocol, 2026-11-08

**GHSA-3g3m-2fjr-6pw4 (glob), Moderate — unresolved — owner decision required.**
Affected installed copies remain `node_modules/glob@10.5.0` and
`node_modules/npm/node_modules/glob@13.0.6`. Root and llmist/CLI/testing development cleanup
scripts declare rimraf `^5.0.5`, resolving to 5.0.10 → glob `^10.3.7`. Release npm 11.21.2
declares glob `^13.0.6`; bundled @npmcli/map-workspaces, @npmcli/package-json and cacache
also declare glob `^13.0.0`. Fresh advisory range `>=9.0.0 <=14.0.1` and registry metadata
place the fixed boundary at 14.0.2, outside all these ranges. Google authentication's
former runtime glob path is removed; cleanup/release copies remain affected.

**GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249 (minimatch), Moderate — unresolved — owner decision required.**
Affected installed copies remain `node_modules/minimatch@9.0.9` and
`node_modules/npm/node_modules/minimatch@10.2.5`. Direct llmist skill filtering declares
`^9.0.9`, inherited by CLI runtime. This remains a potential denial-of-service surface for
pathological patterns. Root/workspace rimraf → glob 10.5.0 declares minimatch `^9.0.4`.
Private documentation directly uses TypeDoc 0.28.17 → minimatch `^9.0.5`; its
typedoc-plugin-markdown 4.10.0 peer and starlight-typedoc 0.22.0 peers reach that same TypeDoc.
Documentation workspace dependency flags do not make this shipped library runtime.
Release npm declares minimatch `^10.2.5`; bundled glob uses `^10.2.2`, @npmcli/arborist,
@npmcli/map-workspaces, ignore-walk and libnpmdiff use `^10.0.3`, and @tufjs/models uses
`^10.1.1`. Fresh advisory range `>=7.0.0 <11.0.1` and registry metadata place the fixed
boundary at 11.0.1, outside each examined range. Semver checks independently confirm the
rimraf/npm glob and direct/TypeDoc/npm minimatch boundaries. No major migration is authorized.

